<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>AAM Arm Care Manual</title>
<style>
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #0F1E35; color: #fff; }
#gate { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: #0F1E35; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; z-index: 999; }
.gate-box { background: #1A2F4E; border-top: 4px solid #C9A84C; padding: 40px; width: min(400px, 90vw); text-align: center; border-radius: 4px; }
.gate-org { color: #C9A84C; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.gate-title { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.gate-sub { color: #8A9BB0; font-size: 13px; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 28px; }
.gate-label { display: block; text-align: left; color: #8A9BB0; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.gate-input { width: 100%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 2px solid #2A4568; color: #fff; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: 6px; padding: 12px; text-align: center; border-radius: 3px; margin-bottom: 14px; outline: none; }
.gate-input:focus { border-color: #C9A84C; }
.gate-btn { width: 100%; background: #C9A84C; color: #0F1E35; border: none; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 14px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
.gate-btn:hover { background: #E4C97A; }
.gate-err { color: #F08070; font-size: 13px; margin-top: 10px; min-height: 18px; }
.gate-footer { color: #3A5A7A; font-size: 11px; margin-top: 18px; }
#app { display: none; min-height: 100vh; background: #F5F4F0; }
.topbar { background: #0F1E35; padding: 0 24px; height: 56px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100; }
.topbar-left { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
.menu-btn { background: none; border: none; color: #fff; font-size: 22px; cursor: pointer; display: none; }
.home-btn { background: none; border: 1px solid #2A4568; color: #C9A84C; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
.page-title { color: #fff; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; }
.topbar-right { color: #4A6A8A; font-size: 11px; text-align: right; }
.layout { display: flex; min-height: calc(100vh - 56px); }
#sidebar { width: 240px; background: #0F1E35; flex-shrink: 0; overflow-y: auto; }
.nav-section { padding: 12px 0 4px; }
.nav-label { color: #2A4A6A; font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0 16px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.nav-item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 8px 16px; color: #7A9AB5; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; border-left: 3px solid transparent; }
.nav-item:hover { color: #fff; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }
.nav-item.active { color: #C9A84C; border-left-color: #C9A84C; background: rgba(201,168,76,0.08); }
.content { flex: 1; padding: 32px 36px; background: #F5F4F0; color: #1C1C1E; max-width: 860px; }
.section { display: none; }
.section.active { display: block; }
.sec-eyebrow { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #C9A84C; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.sec-title { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1E35; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.sec-sub { font-size: 14px; color: #4A4A52; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.gold-bar { height: 2px; background: linear-gradient(to right, #C9A84C, transparent); margin-bottom: 24px; }
.prose p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.78; color: #1C1C1E; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.prose strong { font-weight: 700; color: #0F1E35; }
.h2 { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1E35; margin: 28px 0 10px; padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid #E8E4DC; }
.h3 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1E35; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin: 18px 0 6px; }
.callout { border-radius: 4px; padding: 16px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }
.callout-navy { background: #0F1E35; color: #fff; border-left: 4px solid #C9A84C; }
.callout-navy strong { color: #C9A84C; }
.callout-gold { background: #FDFBF4; border: 1px solid #E8D8A0; border-left: 4px solid #C9A84C; color: #1C1C1E; }
.callout-gold strong { color: #7A6000; }
.callout-warn { background: #FDF2F0; border: 1px solid #F0C0B8; border-left: 4px solid #C8402A; color: #1C1C1E; }
.callout-warn strong { color: #C8402A; }
.callout-green { background: #F0FAF0; border: 1px solid #B0D8B0; border-left: 4px solid #1A6A1A; color: #1C1C1E; }
.ct { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 6px; display: block; }
.callout-navy .ct { color: #C9A84C; }
.callout-warn .ct { color: #C8402A; }
.callout-gold .ct { color: #7A6000; }
.callout-green .ct { color: #1A6A1A; }
.clist { list-style: none; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
.clist li { padding: 4px 0 4px 20px; position: relative; font-size: 14px; color: #1C1C1E; line-height: 1.55; }
.clist li:before { content: "-"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: #C9A84C; font-weight: 700; }
.clist.red li:before { color: #C8402A; }
.std-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; margin: 18px 0; }
.std-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-top: 3px solid #2A4568; padding: 16px; border-radius: 4px; }
.std-card .sct { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #0F1E35; margin-bottom: 5px; }
.std-card .scb { font-size: 13px; color: #4A4A52; line-height: 1.6; }
.rf-group { margin: 14px 0; }
.rf-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #C8402A; margin-bottom: 7px; }
.rf-item { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: #FDF2F0; border: 1px solid #F0C0B8; padding: 9px 13px; border-radius: 3px; margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 13px; color: #1C1C1E; }
.rf-item:before { content: "!"; color: #C8402A; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0; }
.tbl { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0; }
.tbl th { background: #1A2F4E; color: #fff; padding: 9px 12px; text-align: left; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.tbl td { padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #E8E4DC; color: #1C1C1E; vertical-align: top; }
.tbl tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #FAFAF8; }
.int-high { color: #C8402A; font-weight: 700; }
.int-low { color: #1A6A1A; font-weight: 600; }
.int-mid { color: #7A5800; font-weight: 600; }
.wk { font-weight: 700; color: #0F1E35; text-align: center; }
.stars { color: #C9A84C; }
.order-item { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start; padding: 14px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 9px; }
.order-num { background: #0F1E35; color: #C9A84C; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; width: 38px; height: 38px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0; }
.order-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #0F1E35; margin-bottom: 3px; }
.order-desc { font-size: 13px; color: #4A4A52; line-height: 1.6; }
.sb-card { background: #0F1E35; color: #fff; padding: 22px; border-radius: 4px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4,1fr); gap: 18px; margin: 16px 0; }
.sb-item { text-align: center; }
.sb-lbl { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #4A6A8A; margin-bottom: 5px; }
.sb-val { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: #C9A84C; }
.sb-note { font-size: 11px; color: #6A8AAA; margin-top: 3px; }
.rtabs { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.rtab { padding: 7px 16px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; border: 2px solid #E8E4DC; background: #fff; color: #4A4A52; }
.rtab.active { background: #0F1E35; color: #fff; border-color: #0F1E35; }
.rcontent { display: none; }
.rcontent.active { display: block; }
.faq-item { border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 9px; overflow: hidden; }
.faq-q { padding: 14px 18px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #0F1E35; cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #fff; gap: 12px; }
.faq-q:hover { background: #F5F4F0; }
.faq-q.open { background: #0F1E35; color: #fff; }
.faq-tog { color: #C9A84C; font-size: 18px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.faq-a { display: none; padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 13px; color: #1C1C1E; line-height: 1.75; background: #fff; border-top: 1px solid #E8E4DC; }
.faq-a.open { display: block; }
.steps-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px,1fr)); gap: 14px; margin: 16px 0; }
.step-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
.step-hdr { background: #0F1E35; color: #fff; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; padding: 9px 13px; letter-spacing: 1px; }
.step-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 5px 13px; font-size: 13px; border-bottom: 1px solid #F0F0EC; color: #1C1C1E; }
.step-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.step-row.rest { background: #F0F4F8; font-weight: 700; color: #2A4568; font-size: 12px; }
.step-row .dist { color: #0F1E35; font-weight: 700; }
.cal-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(185px,1fr)); gap: 11px; margin: 14px 0; }
.cal-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
.cal-mon { background: #1A2F4E; color: #fff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; padding: 7px 13px; }
.cal-ph { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 5px 13px; }
.cal-bd { font-size: 12px; color: #4A4A52; padding: 0 13px 11px; line-height: 1.5; }
.p-off { background: #E8E4DC; color: #4A4A52; } .p-bld { background: #DAE8F8; color: #1A4A6A; } .p-sea { background: #D8F0E0; color: #1A5A2A; } .p-tr { background: #FDF8DC; color: #6A5800; } .p-del { background: #F2E4D0; color: #6A3A10; } .p-str { background: #1A2F4E; color: #7A9AB5; }
.dis-box { background: #1A2F4E; color: #8A9BB0; font-size: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 4px; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 24px; border: 1px solid #2A4568; }
.dis-box strong { color: #C0D0E0; }
.contact-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-radius: 6px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.contact-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #7A7A85; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.contact-link { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; color: #0F1E35; text-decoration: none; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #F0F0EC; }
.contact-link:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.contact-link:hover { color: #C9A84C; }
.home-hero { background: #0F1E35; padding: 40px 36px; }
.home-hero h1 { color: #fff; font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.home-hero p { color: #7A9AB5; font-size: 14px; font-style: italic; margin: 0; }
.home-bar { height: 3px; background: linear-gradient(to right, #C9A84C, transparent); margin-top: 24px; }
.home-group-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #7A7A85; padding: 20px 36px 10px; }
.home-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px,1fr)); gap: 14px; padding: 0 36px 20px; }
.home-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E8E4DC; border-top: 3px solid transparent; border-radius: 6px; padding: 18px; cursor: pointer; }
.home-card:hover { border-top-color: #C9A84C; }
.home-card .icon { font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.home-card .name { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1E35; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.home-card .desc { font-size: 12px; color: #7A7A85; line-height: 1.5; }
.home-card .tag { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: #C9A84C; margin-top: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; }
@media (max-width: 700px) {
  #sidebar { display: none; position: fixed; top: 56px; left: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 200; width: 240px; }
  #sidebar.open { display: block; }
  .menu-btn { display: block; }
  .content { padding: 20px 16px; }
  .home-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); padding: 0 16px 16px; }
  .home-hero { padding: 28px 16px; }
  .home-group-label { padding: 16px 16px 8px; }
  .std-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .sb-card { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); }
  .cal-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="gate">
  <div class="gate-box">
    <div class="gate-org">Advanced Athletic Medicine</div>
    <div class="gate-title">Arm Care Manual</div>
    <div class="gate-sub">Evidence-Based Standards for the Throwing Athlete</div>
    <label class="gate-label">Access Code</label>
    <input type="password" class="gate-input" id="codeInput" placeholder="* * * * * * *" autocomplete="off">
    <button class="gate-btn" onclick="checkCode()">Enter Program</button>
    <div class="gate-err" id="gateErr"></div>
    <div class="gate-footer">2025 Advanced Athletic Medicine - Individual Use Only</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div id="app">
  <div class="topbar">
    <div class="topbar-left">
      <button class="menu-btn" onclick="toggleMenu()">&#9776;</button>
      <button class="home-btn" onclick="showSection('home')">Home</button>
      <span class="page-title" id="pageTitle">Home</span>
    </div>
    <div class="topbar-right">AAM Arm Care 2025</div>
  </div>
  <div class="layout">
    <div id="sidebar">
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Home</div><div class="nav-item active" onclick="showSection('home')">Home</div></div>
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Foundation</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('why')">Why Arm Care Matters</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('standards')">AAM Standards</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('redflags')">Red Flags</div>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Exercise Library</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('tspine')">T-Spine Mobility</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('foamroll')">Foam Roll</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('stretching')">Static Stretching</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('dynamic')">Dynamic Warm-Up</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('prebands')">Pre-Throw Bands</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('postbands')">Post-Throw Bands</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('scapular')">Scapular Control</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('twoout')">2-Out Drill</div>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Programs</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('gethot')">Get Hot Routine</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('gameday')">Game Day Routines</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('rtt')">Return-to-Throw</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('mound')">Mound Progression</div>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Guidelines</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('pitchcount')">Pitch Count Rules</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('recovery')">Recovery</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('youth')">Youth Arm Care</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('annual')">Annual Planning</div>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Tools</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('readiness')">Arm Readiness Check</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('tracker')">Volume Tracker</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('scheduler')">Weekly Builder</div>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-section"><div class="nav-label">Reference</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('faq')">FAQ</div>
        <div class="nav-item" onclick="showSection('contact')">Contact</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="content" id="contentArea">

      <!-- HOME -->
      <div class="section active" id="sec-home">
        <div class="home-hero"><h1>Arm Care Manual</h1><p>Evidence-Based Standards for the Throwing Athlete - 2025 Edition</p><div class="home-bar"></div></div>
        <div class="home-group-label">Foundation</div>
        <div class="home-grid">
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('why')"><div class="icon">&#128214;</div><div class="name">Why Arm Care Matters</div><div class="desc">Fatigue, preparation, and long-term development</div><div class="tag">Section 1</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('standards')"><div class="icon">&#128203;</div><div class="name">AAM Standards</div><div class="desc">The six principles that guide every training decision</div><div class="tag">Section 2</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('redflags')"><div class="icon">&#9888;</div><div class="name">Red Flags</div><div class="desc">Know when to stop</div><div class="tag">Section 3</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="home-group-label">Exercise Library</div>
        <div class="home-grid">
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('tspine')"><div class="icon">&#128260;</div><div class="name">T-Spine Mobility</div><div class="desc">6 exercises - rotational foundation</div><div class="tag">Daily</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('foamroll')"><div class="icon">&#128307;</div><div class="name">Foam Roll</div><div class="desc">9 areas - full kinetic chain prep</div><div class="tag">Daily</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('stretching')"><div class="icon">&#129336;</div><div class="name">Static Stretching</div><div class="desc">10 stretches - shoulder, hip, pec</div><div class="tag">Daily</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('dynamic')"><div class="icon">&#127939;</div><div class="name">Dynamic Warm-Up</div><div class="desc">17 movements - neuromuscular activation</div><div class="tag">Daily</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('prebands')"><div class="icon">&#128170;</div><div class="name">Pre-Throw Bands</div><div class="desc">15 exercises - activation before mound</div><div class="tag">Pre-Throw</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('postbands')"><div class="icon">&#128257;</div><div class="name">Post-Throw Bands</div><div class="desc">7 isometric holds - restoration</div><div class="tag">Post-Throw</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('scapular')"><div class="icon">&#9898;</div><div class="name">Scapular Control</div><div class="desc">Blackburns, Kendalls, Banded Y</div><div class="tag">Arm Care</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('twoout')"><div class="icon">&#9918;</div><div class="name">2-Out Drill</div><div class="desc">30-45 sec in-game ROM drill</div><div class="tag">In-Game</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="home-group-label">Programs</div>
        <div class="home-grid">
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('gethot')"><div class="icon">&#128293;</div><div class="name">Get Hot Routine</div><div class="desc">Dynamic activation and arm ramp</div><div class="tag">Pre-Game</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('gameday')"><div class="icon">&#127918;</div><div class="name">Game Day Routines</div><div class="desc">SP, RP, Position Player, Catcher</div><div class="tag">Game Day</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('rtt')"><div class="icon">&#128200;</div><div class="name">Return-to-Throw</div><div class="desc">Steps 1-14 - 6 to 8 weeks</div><div class="tag">Program</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('mound')"><div class="icon">&#9968;</div><div class="name">Mound Progression</div><div class="desc">10-week bullpen build</div><div class="tag">Program</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="home-group-label">Tools</div>
        <div class="home-grid">
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('readiness')"><div class="icon">&#128221;</div><div class="name">Arm Readiness Check</div><div class="desc">Post-throw check-in and history</div><div class="tag">Tool</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('tracker')"><div class="icon">&#128202;</div><div class="name">Volume Tracker</div><div class="desc">Log sessions and weekly totals</div><div class="tag">Tool</div></div>
          <div class="home-card" onclick="showSection('scheduler')"><div class="icon">&#128197;</div><div class="name">Weekly Builder</div><div class="desc">Build your custom weekly schedule</div><div class="tag">Tool</div></div>
        </div>
        <div style="height:40px"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- WHY ARM CARE -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-why">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Section 1</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Why Arm Care Matters</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Throwing is one of the most complex and physically demanding movements in sport. It requires precise coordination of the entire body to generate and transfer high levels of force in extremely short time frames. When preparation is insufficient, stress accumulates quickly - most often at the shoulder and elbow.</p>
          <p>In efficient throwing, force is generated from the ground and transferred through the hips, trunk, and shoulder before being expressed through the arm. <strong>The arm functions primarily as a stress receiver and force transmitter, not a primary force generator.</strong> When movement quality, strength, or control is lacking elsewhere in the system, the arm is forced to compensate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy"><strong>Legs - Hips - Core - Shoulder - Arm - Ball</strong><br>Force transfers through the entire chain. Weakness anywhere puts the arm at risk.</div>
        <div class="h2">Fatigue Is a Primary Risk Factor</div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Fatigue is one of the strongest predictors of injury in throwing athletes. It does not always look like exhaustion. Fatigue in a throwing athlete can be subtle: a slightly dropped elbow, a pitch that feels harder to locate, an arm that takes longer than usual to feel loose. These are warning signs that the system is operating under stress it can no longer effectively manage.</p>
          <p>When fatigue accumulates, muscle activation timing becomes delayed, movement patterns become less efficient, and the joints absorb forces they were never designed to handle alone. The arm does not fail because of one bad outing. It fails because stress was repeatedly applied to a system that was not given adequate time to recover.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>Feeling good is not clearance to do more.</strong> It is an opportunity to recover well.</div>
        <div class="h2">Preparation Drives Performance</div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Arm care is not a warmup ritual. It is the work - and when treated as such, performance follows naturally. Athletes who prepare well throw with more efficiency, maintain better mechanics deeper into outings, and recover faster between sessions.</p>
          <p><strong>The focus of any throwing day is throwing.</strong> Arm care prepares the body for that demand - it does not add to it. Every throw before competition is a throw spent. Protect them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="h2">Long-Term Athletic Development</div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>The athletes who reach the highest levels of the game are almost never the ones who threw the most as teenagers. They are the ones who were developed intelligently, protected when it mattered, and given the time and structure to build a body capable of withstanding elite demands.</p>
          <p><strong>Multi-sport participation through high school is one of the most protective things a young athlete can do.</strong> Sport specialization before age 14 has been correlated with higher rates of overuse injury, earlier burnout, and shorter athletic careers.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STANDARDS -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-standards">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Section 2</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">AAM Arm Care Standards</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy"><span class="ct">Core Philosophy</span>Train intelligently and manage stress to support long-term performance and durability. Arm care is not about doing more - it is about doing the right things, consistently.</div>
        <div class="h2">Standards in Practice</div>
        <div class="std-grid">
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Preparation Before Intensity</div><div class="scb">Arm care prepares the body to throw efficiently. Preparation is most critical on hard days - not least critical.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Stress Is Managed, Not Avoided</div><div class="scb">The right amount of stress at the right time, followed by adequate recovery, is exactly how durable throwers are built.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Progressions Are Respected</div><div class="scb">Progression is earned when the body demonstrates it has recovered and adapted. Repeating a stage is never a setback.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Quality Over Quantity</div><div class="scb">Fifty focused, mechanically sound throws does more than one hundred throws without purpose. Every throw should have a reason.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Feedback Guides Adjustment</div><div class="scb">Soreness, stiffness, fatigue, and mechanical changes are all forms of information. Take them seriously.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Consistency Builds Durability</div><div class="scb">Durability is the product of showing up consistently, doing the right things in the right order, and compounding small adaptations over time.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- RED FLAGS -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-redflags">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Section 3</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Red Flags and Athlete Responsibilities</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>We train to throw. We do not throw to train.</strong> Every decision around preparation, recovery, and workload should reflect that principle.</div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn"><span class="ct">Stop Immediately</span>If you experience any of the following, STOP and seek evaluation from an AAM provider or qualified medical professional.</div>
        <div class="rf-group"><div class="rf-label">Pain-Related Red Flags</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Sharp, stabbing, or sudden pain</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Pain that worsens during or after throwing</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Pain that does not improve with rest</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Pain that alters mechanics or movement patterns</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rf-group"><div class="rf-label">Neurological Symptoms</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Numbness or tingling in the arm, hand, or fingers</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Burning sensations</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Loss of coordination or grip strength</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rf-group"><div class="rf-label">Range of Motion or Strength</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Sudden or progressive loss of shoulder or elbow range of motion</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Noticeable weakness not related to normal fatigue</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Inability to fully straighten or bend the elbow</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rf-group"><div class="rf-label">Swelling and Structural Concerns</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Visible swelling around the elbow or shoulder</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Unusual tightness or pressure that does not resolve</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Audible popping or catching accompanied by pain</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rf-group"><div class="rf-label">Unresolved Fatigue</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Persistent arm heaviness</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Loss of throwing feel or control over multiple sessions</div>
          <div class="rf-item">Declining performance despite adequate rest</div>
        </div>
        <div class="h2">Athlete Responsibilities</div>
        <div class="std-grid">
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Train with Awareness</div><div class="scb">Pay attention to how your arm feels during warm-ups, how it responds to intensity, and how it recovers afterward.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Respect Fatigue and Recovery</div><div class="scb">Feeling good after a session does not mean the arm is ready to go harder tomorrow. Recovery happens between sessions.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Communicate Symptoms Early</div><div class="scb">If something feels off - say so. Not after the game. Early communication prevents minor concerns from becoming structural problems.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Never Push Through Pain</div><div class="scb">When pain is present during throwing - not soreness the next morning, but pain during throwing - the session stops. No exceptions.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- EXERCISE PLACEHOLDERS WITH INSTRUCTIONS -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-tspine">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">T-Spine Mobility</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">The thoracic spine is the engine of rotational power in the throwing motion. Without adequate mid-back mobility, the shoulder and elbow are forced to compensate. Complete at the beginning of every session before any throwing begins.</div>
        <div class="h2">Exercises - 1 x 10 each</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Sets x Reps</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Cat / Cow</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Move slowly through flexion and extension with breathing throughout</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Foam Roll Extension</strong></td><td>Each T-Spine level</td><td>Extend over the roller, support head, avoid low back</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Side Lying Open Books</strong></td><td>1 x 10 ea</td><td>Rotate upper arm open, keep knees stacked</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Quadruped T-Spine Rotation</strong></td><td>1 x 10 ea</td><td>Rotate through upper back, hips stay square, reach as far as you can</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Quadruped Thread the Needle</strong></td><td>1 x 10 ea</td><td>Rotate through upper back, hips stay square</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Standing T-Spine Rotation</strong></td><td>1 x 10 ea</td><td>Rotate chest side to side without leaning</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="callout callout-gold">Photos for each exercise coming in the next update.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-foamroll">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Foam Roll</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">Soft tissue preparation increases local blood flow, improves tissue extensibility, and helps identify areas of restriction. The lower body is included intentionally - restriction anywhere in the kinetic chain has consequences at the arm. Move slowly and pause on areas of tension.</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Duration</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Hamstring</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Slow rolls, pause on tight areas; hook uninvolved side if able</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Calf</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Work ankle to knee, hook uninvolved leg for more pressure</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Quad</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Roll hip to knee, controlled pressure</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>IT Band</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Light pressure, slow movement</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Glute</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Cross leg, roll side to side</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Adductor</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Gentle pressure, short range</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Lat</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Side-lying, roll arm pit to mid-back</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>T-Spine Extension</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Roll mid-back only, support neck</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Pec Stretch</strong></td><td>15-30 sec</td><td>Roller parallel to spine, stretching the pec</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-stretching">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Static Stretching</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">Throwing athletes consistently lose range of motion over the course of a season - particularly internal rotation at the throwing shoulder - and this loss is directly associated with increased injury risk. Perform with patience and control. Never force range of motion beyond comfort.</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Stretch</th><th>Sets x Duration</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Active Hamstring</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Extend the leg while holding the back of the thigh throughout</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>3-Way Hamstring</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Stretch in 3 angles: straight, across body, outward</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Side Lying Quad</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>On your side, pull heel toward glute, hips stacked</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Doorway Pec</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Elbow at shoulder height, lean through; try different angles</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Corner Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Lean forward slightly, stretch chest and shoulders</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Modified Sleeper Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Shoulders stacked, pin chin to shoulder, move arm into IR - no forcing, no pain</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Modified Cross Body Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Shoulders stacked, pull arm across chest</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Kneeling Hip Flexor (Couch Stretch)</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Squeeze glute, keep ribs down, shift hips forward using chair</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Frog Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Sit hips back, stretch inner thighs</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>World's Greatest Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 30 sec</td><td>Step forward, rotate toward lead leg, smooth motion</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-dynamic">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Dynamic Warm-Up</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">The dynamic warm-up prepares the neuromuscular system for athletic movement - elevating heart rate, increasing tissue temperature, and reinforcing the movement patterns most relevant to throwing: hip rotation, trunk separation, deceleration, and weight transfer.</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Volume</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Light Jog</strong></td><td>Easy effort</td><td>Easy jog to increase heart rate and body temp</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Back Pedal</strong></td><td>Easy effort</td><td>Upright posture, controlled steps, stay light on the feet</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Lateral Shuffle</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Stay low, chest tall, do not cross feet</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Carioca</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Rotate through the hips and trunk, stay relaxed</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Walking Lunges</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Long stride, knee in line with toes, chest upright</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Reverse Lunge with Rotation</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Step back, rotate toward lead leg, control movement</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Lateral Lunge</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Sit back in hips, keep opposite leg straight, push back to center</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>High Knees</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Drive knees up under control, maintain good posture</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Butt Kicks</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Quick heel to glute motion, stay tall</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Standing Trunk Rotation</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Rotate through the thoracic spine, hips stay mostly forward</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Bent Over Open Books</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Rotate upper body while keeping hips stable</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Hip Hinge and Reach</strong></td><td>1 x 15 yd</td><td>Hinge at hips, neutral spine, reach forward with arms</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Arm Swings Forward to Back</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Relaxed arm motion, full range, not forcing motion</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Arm Swings Side to Side</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Relaxed arm motion, full range, not forcing motion</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Arm Circles Small and Large</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Controlled circles, gradually increase size</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Serratus Push Ups</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Keep arms straight, move shoulder blades only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Shoulder Rolls</strong></td><td>1 x 10 ea</td><td>Smooth rolls forward and backward, relaxed motion</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-prebands">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library - Pre-Throw</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Pre-Throw Bands</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">The final activation step before throwing begins. Purpose: get the muscle groups responsible for throwing firing, primed, and ready before any stress is placed on the arm. One set of 8 reps per exercise. Complete immediately before throwing - after the dynamic warm-up.</div>
        <div class="h3">Wrist and Elbow</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Sets x Reps</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Wrist Flexion</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Neutral hand, palms up, flex the wrist - slow and controlled</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Wrist Extension</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Neutral hand, palms down, extend the wrist - slow and controlled</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Bicep Curl</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Maintain good posture, bend at the elbow, contracting the bicep</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Tricep Extension</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Lock upper arm, extend through the elbow only</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h3">Shoulder and Scapular</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Sets x Reps</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Scaption</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Thumbs up, raise arms to 90 degrees, just outside of neutral</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Low Row</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Pull elbows back, squeeze shoulder blades</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>High Row</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Pull elbows high, avoid shrugging</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>I</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Straight arms, lift with control</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Y</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Lift arms at overhead angle, slow movement</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>T</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Arms out to the side, squeeze between shoulder blades</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Shoulder A</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Elbow level with shoulder, small controlled motion</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Shoulder Extension</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Pull arm back without arching, squeezing shoulder blades</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Shoulder W Robber</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Pull elbows back, rotate hands outward</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Shoulder Adduction</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Pull arm down toward body, control movement</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Overhead Lat Traction Activation</strong></td><td>1 x 8</td><td>Half knee, straight back, pull down and rotate</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-postbands">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library - Post-Throw</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Post-Throw Bands</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">About restoration, not activation. Uses isometric-based exercises - sustained holds rather than through-range movement - to re-establish muscular engagement and begin recovery in a low-stress way. Complete within 30 minutes of finishing a throwing session, every time.</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Sets x Reps x Hold</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>A Hold</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>Arms overhead, hands at the side of your head, hold</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>External Rotation 90/90 Hold</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>Arms at 90/90, sustained hold</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>T Hold</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>Arms out to the side, squeeze shoulder blades and hold</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Shoulder Extension Hold</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>Straight arms, pull shoulder blades back and hold</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Bicep Curl Hold at 90/90</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>At your side, maintain a bicep curl with the shoulder at 90 degrees</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Wrist Flexion Hold</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>At your side, arm straight, flex at the wrist and hold</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Wrist Extension Hold</strong></td><td>1 x 8 x 8-sec hold</td><td>At your side, arm straight, extend the wrist and hold</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-scapular">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Scapular Control</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">Scapular stability is foundational to healthy overhead throwing. These exercises train the scapular stabilizers that control position and movement of the shoulder blade throughout the throwing motion, reducing stress on the rotator cuff and glenohumeral joint.</div>
        <div class="h3">Blackburns</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Sets x Reps</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>T - Thumbs Up</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Prone, thumbs up, set scaps, lift</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>T - Thumbs Neutral</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Prone, thumbs neutral, set scaps, lift</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Y - Thumbs Up</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Prone, thumbs up, set scaps, lift</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Y - Thumbs Neutral</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Prone, thumbs neutral, set scaps, lift</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>External Rotation 90/90</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Prone, shoulder/elbow 90/90, thumbs up, set scaps, externally rotate</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Prone Shoulder Extension Palms Down</strong></td><td>1 x 10</td><td>Prone, set scaps, palms down, straight arms, extend through the shoulder</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h3">Additional Exercises</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Sets x Reps</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Kendalls</strong></td><td>2 x 10</td><td>Balance on stance leg, upright posture, keep arms on wall, slide all the way up and back down</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Banded Y</strong></td><td>2 x 10</td><td>Start hands neutral, set scaps, lift arms into a Y, keeping straight through the elbows</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Reverse Bear Crawls</strong></td><td>2 x 10 yds</td><td>On all fours, set scaps, walk back focusing on the scapular motion</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <div class="section" id="sec-twoout">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Exercise Library - In-Game</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">2-Out Drill</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy">Performed in the dugout when there are 2 outs before returning to the mound. Total time: 30-45 seconds. Limits the range of motion loss that accumulates over the course of an outing. Works because it is done every inning - not selectively.</div>
        <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>Reference:</strong> Escamilla RF, Yamashiro K, et al. Effects of a Short-Duration Stretching Drill After Pitching on Elbow and Shoulder Range of Motion in Professional Baseball Pitchers. Am J Sports Med. 2017;45(3):692-700.</div>
        <table class="tbl" style="margin-top:16px"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Volume</th><th>Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Forearm Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 5 sec</td><td>Gentle stretch, no aggressive pulling</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Cross Body Stretch</strong></td><td>3 x 5 sec</td><td>Relax shoulder, pull across body at the elbow</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Swims</strong></td><td>1 x 5</td><td>Smooth arm circles through full range</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Field Goals</strong></td><td>1 x 5</td><td>Elbows at 90 degrees, palms neutral, ER at the shoulder then press up</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Hugs</strong></td><td>1 x 5</td><td>Wrap arms around chest, open wide</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Arm Circles Small and Large</strong></td><td>1 x 5 ea way</td><td>Controlled speed, full motion - small and large, CW and CCW</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Bent Over Trunk Rotation</strong></td><td>1 x 5 ea</td><td>Rotate chest side to side, stay hinged</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <!-- GET HOT -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-gethot">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Programs - Pre-Game</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Get Hot Routine</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="h2">Dynamic Activation</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Deep Breath</strong></td><td>4 sec inhale, 4 sec hold, 8 sec exhale</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Scissor Jumps</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Side to Side Jumps</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Lateral Shuffle and Stick</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Reverse Lunge with Rotation</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>A Skips</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Hip Swings</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Bent Over Trunk Rotation</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Banded External Rotation</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Banded Low Row</strong></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Scap Push Ups</strong></td><td></td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h2">Arm Ramp</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Volume</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Light Plyo Throw or Wrist Flick</strong></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Short Catch</strong></td><td>6-8 throws</td><td>30-45 feet, 60-70% intent</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Reverse Throws</strong></td><td>1 x 4</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Decel Throws</strong></td><td>1 x 4</td><td></td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h2">Mound Transition</div>
        <ul class="clist"><li>3 Fastballs at 70%</li><li>2 Fastballs at 85%</li><li>1 Fastball at Game Intent</li><li>1-2 Secondary Pitches if time allows</li></ul>
        <div class="callout callout-warn" style="margin-top:16px"><strong>Key Rules:</strong> Do not throw just to throw. No full bullpens to get loose. Stop once you are hot.</div>
      </div>

      <!-- GAME DAY -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-gameday">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Programs - Game Day</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Game Day Routines</h1>
        <div class="sec-sub">Position-specific warm-up protocols to reach competitive readiness in the fewest throws</div>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>The number one mistake athletes make on game day is throwing too much before they throw competitively.</strong> Every throw before competition is a throw spent.</div>
        <div class="rtabs">
          <div class="rtab active" onclick="showRoutine('sp',this)">Starting Pitcher</div>
          <div class="rtab" onclick="showRoutine('rp',this)">Relief Pitcher</div>
          <div class="rtab" onclick="showRoutine('pos',this)">Position Player</div>
          <div class="rtab" onclick="showRoutine('cat',this)">Catcher</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rcontent active" id="routine-sp">
          <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>Total pre-game pitches should not exceed 30-35.</strong></div>
          <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Activity</th><th>Volume</th><th>Intent</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td class="wk">1</td><td>Dynamic Warm-Up</td><td>Full routine</td><td>-</td><td>Complete before any throwing begins</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">2</td><td>J-Band Pre-Throw Routine</td><td>1 x 8 each</td><td>-</td><td>Full pre-throw band series</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">3</td><td>Flat ground - easy toss</td><td>20-25 throws at 45-60 ft</td><td>40-50%</td><td>Focus on loosening, not effort</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">4</td><td>Flat ground - building</td><td>10-15 throws at 60-90 ft</td><td>60-70%</td><td>Gradual intensity increase</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">5</td><td>Flat ground - crow hop</td><td>5-8 throws at 90 ft</td><td>75-80%</td><td>Simulate game-effort mechanics</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">6</td><td>Mound - fastball only</td><td>8-10 pitches</td><td>80-85%</td><td>Work on release, not max velo</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">7</td><td>Mound - full repertoire</td><td>10-12 pitches</td><td>85-90%</td><td>Off-speed included, game-ready</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">8</td><td>Rest and stay warm</td><td>Until game time</td><td>-</td><td>Light movement, stay loose</td></tr>
          </tbody></table>
        </div>
        <div class="rcontent" id="routine-rp">
          <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>Track all bullpen activity.</strong> Relievers who warm up 2-3 times without entering accumulate significant invisible throwing volume.</div>
          <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Activity</th><th>Volume</th><th>Intent</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td class="wk">1</td><td>Bands abbreviated</td><td>8 reps key exercises</td><td>-</td><td>Scaption, rows, ER</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">2</td><td>Easy flat ground</td><td>8-10 throws at 45 ft</td><td>40-50%</td><td>Get the arm moving quickly</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">3</td><td>Building toss</td><td>8-10 throws at 60-75 ft</td><td>65-75%</td><td>Increase intent steadily</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">4</td><td>Mound - fastball</td><td>6-8 pitches</td><td>85-90%</td><td>Hard and fast - game ready</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">5</td><td>Mound - full repertoire</td><td>4-6 pitches</td><td>90-95%</td><td>Off-speed to confirm feel</td></tr>
          </tbody></table>
        </div>
        <div class="rcontent" id="routine-pos">
          <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Activity</th><th>Volume</th><th>Intent</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td class="wk">1</td><td>Dynamic Warm-Up</td><td>Full routine</td><td>-</td><td>Do not skip for position players</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">2</td><td>Abbreviated J-Band</td><td>5-6 exercises x 8 reps</td><td>-</td><td>Low row, ER, scaption, rows</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">3</td><td>Catch - easy</td><td>10-12 throws at 45 ft</td><td>50%</td><td>Easy pace, feel the ball</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">4</td><td>Catch - building</td><td>8-10 throws at 60-90 ft</td><td>65-75%</td><td>Increase to position-appropriate distance</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">5</td><td>Position-specific throws</td><td>5-8 throws</td><td>80-90%</td><td>Simulate game throws from position</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">6</td><td>Full effort rep</td><td>2-3 throws</td><td>90-95%</td><td>One all-out throw from position</td></tr>
          </tbody></table>
        </div>
        <div class="rcontent" id="routine-cat">
          <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>Catchers should complete the full post-throw band routine after every game and practice.</strong></div>
          <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Activity</th><th>Volume</th><th>Intent</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td class="wk">1</td><td>Full dynamic warm-up</td><td>Complete</td><td>-</td><td>Include hip mobility</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">2</td><td>Full J-Band series</td><td>Pre-throw complete</td><td>-</td><td>Never skip for catchers</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">3</td><td>Flat ground easy</td><td>10-12 at 45 ft</td><td>40-50%</td><td>Easy movement</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">4</td><td>Flat ground building</td><td>8-10 at 60-75 ft</td><td>65-70%</td><td>Build toward throw-down distance</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">5</td><td>Crouch throws</td><td>5-6 throws</td><td>75-80%</td><td>Simulate throw-down mechanics</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">6</td><td>Full effort throw-downs</td><td>3-5 throws</td><td>90-95%</td><td>Second base distance, full effort</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="wk">7</td><td>Pop time check</td><td>1-2 throws</td><td>100%</td><td>Confirm readiness</td></tr>
          </tbody></table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- RTT -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-rtt">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Programs</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Return-to-Throw Program</h1>
        <div class="sec-sub">Interval throwing - Steps 1-14</div>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn"><span class="ct">Do Not Advance If:</span>Pain during or after throwing - Soreness beyond 24-36 hrs - Mechanical breakdown - Declining arm speed - Incomplete recovery. <strong>Repeating a stage is always safer than rushing forward.</strong></div>
        <ul class="clist" style="margin-bottom:18px"><li>Program typically takes 6-8 weeks to complete</li><li>Throwing days every other day</li><li>Feeling good does not mean the arm is ready to advance</li></ul>
        <div class="h2">Steps 1-11 - Interval Throwing</div>
        <div class="steps-grid" id="rtt-steps"></div>
        <div class="h2">Steps 12-14 - Positional Players</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>Step 12</th><th>Step 13</th><th>Step 14</th><th>Return to Normal</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>45 ft</td><td>5-10</td><td>5-10</td><td>5-10</td><td rowspan="5" style="vertical-align:middle;font-weight:700;color:#0F1E35">Normal Volume</td></tr>
          <tr><td>60 ft</td><td>5-10</td><td>5-10</td><td>5-10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>90 ft</td><td>5-10</td><td>5-10</td><td>5-10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>105 ft</td><td>10</td><td>10</td><td>10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>120 ft</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>15</td></tr>
          <tr><td>135 ft</td><td>10</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Position Based</td><td>-</td><td>20 throws</td><td>20-30 throws</td><td>Full Return</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <!-- MOUND -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-mound">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Programs - Pitchers</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Mound Progression</h1>
        <div class="sec-sub">Weeks 1-10 following the Interval Throwing Program</div>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;width:60px">Week</th><th>Activity</th><th style="width:80px">Volume</th><th style="width:90px">Intent</th><th>Goal</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td class="wk">1</td><td>Flat Ground</td><td style="text-align:center">20</td><td class="int-low">50%</td><td>Reintroduce throwing mechanics, rhythm, and basic arm tolerance</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">2</td><td>Flat Ground</td><td style="text-align:center">20-25</td><td class="int-mid">50-70%</td><td>Build consistency and repeatability while gradually increasing intent</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">3</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">15</td><td class="int-low">50%</td><td>Restore mound familiarity at low intent</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">4</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">30</td><td class="int-low">50%</td><td>Increase mound volume without increasing intensity</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">5</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">45</td><td class="int-mid">50-70%</td><td>Introduce controlled intent while maintaining clean mechanics</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">6</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">60</td><td class="int-mid">70%</td><td>Increase mound intent while preserving arm elasticity</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">7</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">20</td><td class="int-high">100%</td><td>First exposure to full intent at intentionally low volume</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">8</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">30</td><td class="int-high">100%</td><td>Prepare CNS for sustained full-intent throwing</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">9</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">40</td><td class="int-high">100%</td><td>Transition to competitive throwing</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="wk">10</td><td>Bullpen</td><td style="text-align:center">50</td><td class="int-high">100%</td><td>Build volume to withstand normal workloads</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="callout callout-navy" style="margin-top:18px"><strong>Intent refers to effort level, not velocity.</strong> Velocity should never be chased during this program.</div>
      </div>

      <!-- PITCH COUNT -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-pitchcount">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Guidelines</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Pitch Count Rules</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn"><span class="ct">These Are Minimums - Not Targets</span>An athlete who has thrown 75 pitches may still need more than 4 days of rest based on fatigue. Use pitch count as a floor, not a ceiling.</div>
        <div class="h2">Pitch Count Limits by Age</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Age</th><th>Max / Day</th><th>Recommended</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>7-8</td><td>50</td><td>35-40</td><td>Motor pattern development priority</td></tr>
          <tr><td>9-10</td><td>75</td><td>50-60</td><td>First exposure to velocity training; watch mechanics</td></tr>
          <tr><td>11-12</td><td>85</td><td>60-70</td><td>Growth plate vulnerability; strict limits recommended</td></tr>
          <tr><td>13-14</td><td>95</td><td>70-80</td><td>Elbow growth plate most vulnerable; watch for pain</td></tr>
          <tr><td>15-16</td><td>95</td><td>75-85</td><td>UCL risk increases; begin formal arm care program</td></tr>
          <tr><td>17-18</td><td>105</td><td>80-90</td><td>Near skeletal maturity; still monitor closely</td></tr>
          <tr><td>19+</td><td>No formal limit</td><td>85-100</td><td>Fatigue-based limits apply</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h2">Required Rest Days</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Pitches Thrown</th><th>Required Rest</th><th>AAM Recommendation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>1-20</td><td>0 days</td><td>1 day minimum</td></tr>
          <tr><td>21-35</td><td>1 day</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>36-50</td><td>2 days</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>51-65</td><td>3 days</td><td>3-4 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>66-80</td><td>4 days</td><td>4-5 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>81-95</td><td>5 days</td><td>5-6 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>96-105 (17-18 only)</td><td>6 days</td><td>6-7 days</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <!-- RECOVERY -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-recovery">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Guidelines</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Recovery Protocols</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-gold"><strong>The most effective recovery tools are also the simplest:</strong> sleep, hydration, and nutrition. No modality compensates for chronic sleep deprivation or poor fueling.</div>
        <div class="h2">Ice vs Heat</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Modality</th><th>When to Use</th><th>Duration</th><th>Avoid When</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Ice</strong></td><td>Immediately post-throwing within 30 min</td><td>10-15 min</td><td>Before throwing - reduces proprioception</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Heat</strong></td><td>Pre-throwing, day after soreness</td><td>10-15 min</td><td>Immediately post-throwing</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Contrast</strong></td><td>2+ days post-outing for residual soreness</td><td>10 min each x 2</td><td>Acute injury, less than 24 hrs post-outing</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h2">Sleep by Age Group</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Age</th><th>Recommended</th><th>Minimum</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>13-17</td><td>9-10 hours</td><td>8 hours</td></tr>
          <tr><td>18-22</td><td>8-9 hours</td><td>7 hours</td></tr>
          <tr><td>22+</td><td>7-9 hours</td><td>7 hours</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h2">Nutrition Timing</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Timing</th><th>What to Consume</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>2-3 hrs before</td><td>Balanced meal: carbs, protein, low fat</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Within 30 min post-throw</td><td>20-30g protein + simple carbs</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Within 2 hours</td><td>Complete meal: protein, complex carbs, vegetables</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Throughout day</td><td>Half bodyweight in lbs = oz of water daily</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="h2">Evidence-Based Modalities</div>
        <table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Modality</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Best Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Sleep</strong></td><td><span class="stars">*****</span></td><td>Every recovery day - non-negotiable</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Hydration</strong></td><td><span class="stars">*****</span></td><td>Daily and intra-competition</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Post-throw nutrition</strong></td><td><span class="stars">****</span></td><td>20-30g protein within 30 min</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Light active recovery</strong></td><td><span class="stars">****</span></td><td>Walking, bike, swim - day after high-load</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Static stretching post-throw</strong></td><td><span class="stars">****</span></td><td>Critical for maintaining ROM over a season</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Cold water immersion</strong></td><td><span class="stars">***</span></td><td>10-15 min post-competition</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>BFR low load</strong></td><td><span class="stars">***</span></td><td>Post-throw recovery only; no added load</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Massage and foam roll</strong></td><td><span class="stars">***</span></td><td>Day after or between outings</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>

      <!-- YOUTH -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-youth">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Guidelines</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Youth Arm Care</h1>
        <div class="sec-sub">For Little League athletes and parents</div>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="callout callout-navy"><strong>We Train to Throw - Not Throw to Train.</strong> A strong arm starts with a strong body.</div>
        <div class="h2">5 Youth Arm Care Rules</div>
        <div class="std-grid">
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">1. Pain Is NOT Normal</div><div class="scb">Soreness after activity can happen. Pain while throwing is different. If your child says their elbow hurts or arm feels dead - stop throwing immediately.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">2. Fatigue Changes Everything</div><div class="scb">Tired athletes move differently. When mechanics break down, injury risk goes up. Signs include throwing slower, dropping elbow, arm feeling heavy.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">3. More Throwing Is NOT Better</div><div class="scb">Kids do not improve by endlessly throwing. Smart training beats extra volume. Quality over quantity.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">4. Recovery Is Part of Training</div><div class="scb">Drink water, get sleep, eat protein, take rest days. Recovery helps the arm rebuild. Healthy habits matter.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">5. Speak Up Early</div><div class="scb">Small issues become big problems when ignored. Early evaluation equals faster return and fewer missed games. Speaking up is not weakness.</div></div>
          <div class="std-card"><div class="sct">Parents: Your Role</div><div class="scb">Help your athlete listen to their body, be honest about pain, respect rest days, and communicate with coaches and providers.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout callout-green" style="margin-top:20px"><span class="ct">Game Day Checklist</span>Did I sleep well? Did I eat? Did I warm up? Does my arm feel normal?<br><br><strong>If any answer is NO - talk to an adult before throwing.</strong></div>
      </div>

      <!-- ANNUAL PLANNING -->
      <div class="section" id="sec-annual">
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Guidelines</div>
        <h1 class="sec-title">Annual Planning</h1>
        <div class="gold-bar"></div>
        <div class="cal-grid">
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">January</div><div class="cal-ph p-off">Off-Season Shutdown</div><div class="cal-bd">Complete rest from throwing. Body recovery and general fitness only.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">February</div><div class="cal-ph p-bld">Build-Up Phase 1</div><div class="cal-bd">RTT Steps 1-5. Light toss, arm care daily.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">March</div><div class="cal-ph p-bld">Build-Up Phase 2</div><div class="cal-bd">Steps 6-11. Bullpen begins. Flat ground to mound Weeks 1-4.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">April</div><div class="cal-ph p-sea">In-Season</div><div class="cal-bd">Competitive season. Pitch count compliance. Maintenance arm care.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">May</div><div class="cal-ph p-sea">In-Season</div><div class="cal-bd">Peak competition. Monitor workload closely. Weekly volume tracking.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">June</div><div class="cal-ph p-sea">Late Season</div><div class="cal-bd">Manage fatigue. Reduce non-game throwing.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">July</div><div class="cal-ph p-tr">Transition</div><div class="cal-bd">Structured rest 2-4 weeks first. Limit to one program at a time.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">August</div><div class="cal-ph p-tr">Transition</div><div class="cal-bd">Monitor cumulative volume. Begin deload if summer ball ending.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">September</div><div class="cal-ph p-del">Deload</div><div class="cal-bd">Significant reduction in throwing. Arm care and conditioning only.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">October</div><div class="cal-ph p-str">Off-Season Strength</div><div class="cal-bd">No throwing. Strength, mobility, and movement training focus.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">November</div><div class="cal-ph p-str">Off-Season Strength</div><div class="cal-bd">Continue strength block. Light throwing late month if desired.</div></div>
          <div class="cal-card"><div class="cal-mon">December</div><div class="cal-ph p-off">Off-Season Shutdown</div><div class="cal-bd">Full rest or light maintenance. Prepare for January reset.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

